<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermeric</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 441</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermeric was king of the Suebi who led his people across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in 406 and into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> in 409. In 411 they received lands in Gallaecia, where he founded the Suebic kingdom with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bracara-augusta">Bracara Augusta</a>. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> and the local Hispano-Roman population, and in 438 handed power to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rechila">Rechila</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hermeric.jpg" alt="Hermeric" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O_rei_suevo_Hermerico_no_Corpus_Pelagianum_(BNE_Mss_1513).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
